# Chromium test: race between document.cookie setter (CookieJar mojo pipe, async
# with AsyncSetCookie) and cookieStore.get() (CookieStore API, separate mojo pipe).
# These use independent RestrictedCookieManager pipes with no ordering guarantee.
# Brave's ephemeral storage checks (FillEphemeralStorageParams,
# IsEphemeralCookieAccessible) add processing overhead that widens the race window.
# Stable upstream: 0.2% flake rate over 30 days per LUCI Analysis.
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/55325
-All/CookieStoreSameSiteTest.CookieStoreUsesEffectiveSameSiteForUnspecifiedCookies/0
-All/CookieStoreSameSiteTest.CookieStoreUsesEffectiveSameSiteForUnspecifiedCookies/1

# Chromium test: intermittent RunLoop timeout in DevTools paused debugger focus
# mechanism. The test relies on an async chain (DebuggerPaused event → SourcesPanel
# module loading → bringToFront IPC) that sometimes doesn't complete before the
# test timeout. Already disabled upstream on Windows ASAN (crbug.com/337141755).
# 0.2% upstream flake rate over 30 days per LUCI Analysis. No Brave-specific code
# affects this path.
# https://github.com/brave/brave-browser/issues/53358
-DevToolsProcessPerSiteTest.PausedDebuggerFocus

